---
title: Sweet potato casserole
servings: 8
tags: [american, vegetarian, thanksgiving, holiday, fall]
cuisine: american
source: Adapted from Sweet Potato Casserole in tdstein/recipes (MIT), https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tdstein/recipes/main/recipes/Sweet%20Potato%20Casserole.cook
---

Heat the oven to 350°F. Grease a #9-by-13-inch baking dish{} with @unsalted butter{2%tbsp}.

Bake the @sweet potatoes{4%lb} on a #baking sheet{} about ~{1%hour}, until soft all the way through. Peel them and mash the flesh in a #large bowl{}.

Beat in @unsalted butter{1/2%cup}, @eggs{2}, @sweetened condensed milk{14%oz}, @granulated sugar{1/4%cup}, @vanilla extract{1%tsp} and @salt{1%tsp}. Spread it in the dish.

== Topping ==

Stir together the @pecans{1%cup}(finely chopped), @cornflakes{1%cup}(lightly crushed, optional), @dark brown sugar{1/2%cup}, @all-purpose flour{1/2%cup} and @unsalted butter{1/4%cup}(melted). Scatter it over the potatoes.

Bake ~{35%minutes}, until lightly browned.

Cover the top with @marshmallows{2%cups}(mini) and bake ~{5%minutes} more, until they melt and toast. Rest ~{5%minutes} before serving.
